<PageLayout title="About" heading="About My Dutch Door" description="My Dutch Door helps non-EU expats, mainly US citizens, find an independent mortgage adviser in the Netherlands." dek="Your way into a Dutch home.">
  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>Buying a home in the Netherlands as a non-EU expat raises questions Dutch buyers never have to ask: residence permits, how banks treat a US passport under FATCA, income paid in dollars, the expat ruling. Good answers are hard to find in plain English.</p>
  <p>My Dutch Door explains these topics in guides that a licensed mortgage adviser reviews, and connects you with an independent adviser when you are ready to talk.</p>
  <h2>What we are, and what we are not</h2>
  <p>My Dutch Door is an introduction service. We do not give mortgage advice, we are not a lender and we are not a mortgage adviser. When you send a request, we pass your contact details to one independent mortgage advisory partner, whose advisers contact you directly.</p>
